      "Development of advanced materials concepts in light water reactor nuclear engineering systems. This includes foundational concepts such as radiation damage, corrosion, and the materials systems found in light water reactors. Advanced concepts include kinetic rate theory, evolution of irradiated microstructures, water chemistry control, stress corrosion cracking, radiation induced segregation, and other phenomenon associated with radiation damage are introduced. Advanced microanalytical analysis techniques will be presented, as will computational approaches applicable to the study of radiation damage in metals. Materials for use in advanced reactor concepts will be presented.",
